;; The jurisdiction-independent layer: what ROLES a recovery system needs
;; somebody to play, and the open normative minima that apply everywhere.
;;
;; Every other file in this directory is a binding of these roles to the
;; instruments one place actually has. A role with no local binding is not a
;; formatting gap -- it is the finding. Where nothing issues a damage
;; certificate, nothing downstream of the certificate can be gated on one,
;; and the recovery either finds another trigger for money and demolition or
;; it does not have one.
{:profile/id :global
 :profile/kind :role-vocabulary
 :profile/label {:ja "共通（役割の語彙）" :en "Global (role vocabulary)"}

 :profile/instrument-roles
 [{:instrument/id :instrument/none
   :ja "制度による前提なし" :en "No instrument gates this"}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/relief-act
   :ja "災害救助の発動" :en "Statutory relief activation"
   :role "The legal act that makes publicly funded shelter, temporary housing and
          emergency repair possible at all. Almost everything else waits on its date."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/severe-disaster
   :ja "激甚災害等の上乗せ指定" :en "Severe-disaster escalation"
   :role "A second designation that raises the share of cost carried above the local
          authority. Its absence is what bankrupts small municipalities."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/damage-certificate
   :ja "被害の公的認定（罹災証明に相当するもの）" :en "Official per-building damage determination"
   :role "A per-building, appealable determination of damage severity. The pivot of the
          whole system: cash, demolition, tax relief and often insurance hang off it,
          which is why its throughput -- not its policy -- sets the recovery's pace."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/household-grant
   :ja "被災世帯への給付" :en "Household recovery grant"
   :role "Non-repayable money to a household, banded by the damage determination."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/emergency-repair
   :ja "住宅の応急修理" :en "Emergency habitability repair"
   :role "Public payment for the minimum repair that lets people live at home again.
          Where it exists it empties the temporary-housing queue from the other end."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/public-demolition
   :ja "公費解体" :en "Publicly funded demolition"
   :role "Public demolition and disposal of a privately owned damaged building.
          Requires both the damage determination and clear title or consent -- the
          second requirement is the one that stalls informal and inherited housing."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/business-grant
   :ja "事業再建の補助・融資" :en "Business recovery grant or lending"}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/insurance
   :ja "水災補償" :en "Flood insurance or mutual-aid cover"
   :role "Private or public-private cover for flood loss. Penetration, not existence,
          is what matters, and it varies by two orders of magnitude between places."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/volunteer-coordination
   :ja "ボランティアの調整主体" :en "Volunteer coordination body"
   :role "Whoever converts arriving goodwill into matched, insured, briefed work.
          Where nobody plays this role, labour arrives and does not become throughput."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/waste-plan
   :ja "災害廃棄物処理の計画と用地" :en "Disaster waste plan and land"
   :role "Authority to open temporary storage sites and contract haulage at scale.
          The scarce input is land, and land cannot be surged after the fact."}
  {:instrument/id :instrument/temporary-housing
   :ja "応急的な住まいの供給" :en "Temporary housing supply"
   :role "Purpose-built units, leased private rentals, or cash for rent. Which of the
          three a place can use is the single largest driver of shelter duration."}]

 ;; Sphere Handbook 2018 minimum standards, cited as an open reference framework
 ;; (NOT a membership claim -- same posture as actor-kazaori G9). These are
 ;; normative floors for the displacement phase, not parameters of the model.
 :profile/sphere-minima
 [{:id :sphere/water-quantity :value 15 :unit "litre/person/day"
   :source "Sphere Handbook 2018, WASH -- Water supply standard 2.1"
   :note "Basic survival quantity for drinking, cooking and personal hygiene."}
  {:id :sphere/covered-living-space :value 3.5 :unit "m2/person"
   :source "Sphere Handbook 2018, Shelter and settlement standard 3"
   :note "Minimum covered living area, excluding cooking and sanitation space."}
  {:id :sphere/shared-toilet-ratio :value 20 :unit "person/toilet"
   :source "Sphere Handbook 2018, WASH -- Excreta management standard 3.2"
   :note "Maximum people sharing one toilet; sex-separated and safely reachable."}]

 ;; What actually differs between places, once the structure is held constant.
 ;; These are the axes a new jurisdiction profile should answer.
 :profile/variation-axes
 [{:axis :axis/climate
   :ja "気候（乾燥速度と季節）" :en "Climate: how fast a wet building dries, and when"
   :effect "Binds ambient_dry_rate and therefore the mold split. A monsoon recovery and
            a temperate autumn recovery are not the same problem with different labels."}
  {:axis :axis/construction
   :ja "建築構法" :en "Construction type"
   :effect "Timber frame with plasterboard and mineral-wool insulation must be stripped
            and dried or it is written off. Masonry and concrete tolerate wetting but
            hide contamination. Informal construction is usually a total loss."}
  {:axis :axis/tenure
   :ja "権利関係（登記・借家・非正規）" :en "Tenure: title, tenancy, informality"
   :effect "The damage-certificate and public-demolition path assumes an identifiable
            owner. Where households have no registered title, the entire entitlement
            branch of this model is unavailable to exactly the people worst hit."}
  {:axis :axis/insurance-penetration
   :ja "水災補償の普及率" :en "Flood-cover penetration"
   :effect "Decides whether reconstruction is financed privately, publicly, or not at all."}
  {:axis :axis/labour-model
   :ja "労働力の供給モデル" :en "Where the labour comes from"
   :effect "Coordinated civilian volunteering, contracted market labour, NGO cluster
            deployment, or military engineering. Each has a different arrival curve and
            a different ceiling, and the volunteer-centre parameters mean different
            things in each."}
  {:axis :axis/waste-siting
   :ja "仮置場の事前選定の有無" :en "Whether waste sites were designated in advance"
   :effect "Pre-designated sites turn a three-week search into a day-one opening, which
            is the difference between waste at a site and waste on the road."}]}
